        <blank line>
        Pass the ``turn_started_at``/``turn_event_id`` returned by
        ``start_turn`` or ``continue_turn``. Call this once per terminal —
        the host polls status every two seconds and should read cost once,
        not on every poll. Returns ``{"cost_usd": "<decimal string>" | None,
        "event_count": <int>}``. ``cost_usd`` is ``None`` when the session's
        model has no pricing row (never zero — zero would falsely claim the
        turn was free). This figure is NOT expected to equal the tenant
        ledger's debit for the same turn: the ledger applies
        ``settings.billing.markup`` on top of it.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'handle': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'turn_event_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'turn_started_at': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'handle',
          'turn_started_at',
          'turn_event_id',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'github_connect': dict({
      'description': '''
        Give this agent token access to more repos, such as a private GitHub repo.
        <blank line>
        Use this when someone asks to let an agent read a private repository
        at github.com/owner/repo. Show a single-use
        connection button bound to the selected agent to an admin; repos
        connected this way are for that agent only. Other members get Ask an
        admin and a recorded request. The card may go to the requester's
        private chat instead; the result says so. Never repeat a private link in a
        shared reply. For a setup
        target, pass its current name and MA id from turn_controls; otherwise
        this defaults to the responder.
        When GitHub access interrupted a task, pass a short restatement as
        requested_work so the task resumes after connection. Leave it empty
        when someone only asks to connect GitHub.
        For a clear 'give this agent access to owner/repo', call with repo_name
        right away; don't ask for a yes first. Ask only if the repo or agent is
        unclear. confirmed is ignored. A connected repo is granted
        directly when this person may grant it. Otherwise the single Connect
        GitHub link lets them connect that repo in a browser. Connecting repos
        gives token access; it does not put them all in the filesystem.
        After it posts, nothing is connected until the person saves on the page.
        The card carries the steps: never repeat them, and never say done or connected.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'agent_name': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'confirmed': dict({
            'default': False,
            'type': 'boolean',
          }),
          'expected_ma_agent_id': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'default': '',
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'repo_name': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'requested_work': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
        }),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'hand_off_task': dict({
      'description': '''
        Hand this task over to another agent in the same conversation: "have that one take over", "let churn-explorer finish this".
        <blank line>
        `set_setup_target` changes your configuration target; `set_agent_default`
        changes who answers a channel; neither does this. The destination must
        already answer in this workspace. A member may hand only to an agent of
        this channel (the one it answers with, or one pinned to it); any other
        needs an admin.
        <blank line>
        From the next message here, that agent answers, with its own keys,
        connections and memory; conversation, decisions and files move with the
        requester. Posted files stay posted. No extra billed turn unless
        `continuation` is set.
        <blank line>
        `origin_context_id` must name this execution's origin and match the
        calling session's signed grant. Empty IDs and other sessions' origins
        refuse, even for the same account and agent. Attendance comes from
        that verified origin; queueing work does not grant human approval.
        <blank line>
        `agent_id`: the destination's current id from `list_agents`; a recreated
        namesake is refused. `continuation` is null unless the person asked the
        destination to continue or finish NAMED work ("let it finish the chart").
        "Take over" alone is switch-only — null. Never restate finished work. A
        too-short, empty, or name-only value is auto-nulled — get the wording
        right regardless.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'agent_id': dict({
            'description': "The destination agent's current MA id, e.g. agt_01…",
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'continuation': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': "Null unless the person explicitly asked the destination to continue or finish NAMED work, in their own words. 'Take over' alone, with no named work, is null. Never restate work that already finished.",
          }),
          'keep_provider': dict({
            'default': False,
            'description': 'True only for a new copy of you that should stay on your model provider. A copy being switched to another provider is handed the thread after its switch card is approved, never before.',
            'type': 'boolean',
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'unsaved_work': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'enum': list([
                  'copy',
                  'leave',
                ]),
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': 'Only after the person answers the uncommitted-work question.',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'origin_context_id',
          'agent_id',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
