        'required': list([
          'thread_id',
          'name',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'replace_channel_file': dict({
      'description': '''
        Save an edited file over a Teams channel file as its new version.
        <blank line>
        Use this when asked to update, fix or edit a file that is already in
        the channel's Files, instead of posting a renamed copy. Download the
        current file, edit it, stage the result with
        ``create_file_upload_url`` (PUT the bytes) and pass that
        ``file_handle``, of the same file type.
        <blank line>
        ``link`` and ``version`` come together from where you downloaded the
        file: an ``[attachment]`` line or ``<attachment>`` element of this
        conversation, or a file of read_channel, read_thread or get_message.
        ``channel_id`` is this conversation's channel or thread id and
        ``origin_context_id`` this turn's, from turn_controls: only a file
        inside the Files folder of the channel this turn started in can be
        replaced, and you must be able to post there.
        <blank line>
        SharePoint keeps every earlier version, so an edit can be restored.
        Refusals say what to do: a file changed since you read it is not
        overwritten (download it again and redo the edit); a file open in a
        desktop app is locked; a permission, retention policy or sensitivity
        label can block the write. Then post your version as a new file with
        send_message instead. If saving did not finish, read the channel
        before trying again: it may have been saved. Put the returned
        ``markdown`` line in your reply as it is: it opens the file in Office
        for the web. To replace it again, pass the returned ``link`` and
        ``version``.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'channel_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'file_handle': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'link': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'version': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'channel_id',
          'link',
          'version',
          'file_handle',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'request_agent_backend_switch': dict({
      'description': '''
        Preview a requested agent backend switch, then Confirm in this chat.
        <blank line>
        Use when an admin or the agent's owner asks to switch it to Anthropic, OpenAI
        or Gemini,
        optionally naming a model naturally: "switch Researcher to argon" or
        "switch Researcher to luna". For an Anthropic model change such as
        "set Writer to opus 5.5", use update_agent with that natural model name.
        ``model`` accepts natural names or one of
        the returned ``models``; omit it for the provider's default. A provider
        alone ("switch to GPT", "to Gemini") means its default: omit ``model`` and
        preview; never ask which model. Never ask the person for a model id.
        Ambiguous model names return the choices.
        The switch applies to
        new conversations wherever the agent answers, and to this conversation
        from the next message when the switched agent answers here (the result's
        summary says which). The server's default or built-in agent switches only
        when the person says it's for everyone (for_everyone=true, on both calls);
        otherwise offer the copy below. For "make a copy of yourself on Gemini":
        copy the agent with fork_agent and new_copy_if_taken=true (always a NEW
        copy, never an earlier one; use the name it returns from here on), then
        switch the copy here. Don't hand_off_task first: the confirmed switch hands
        this conversation to the copy and moves it to Gemini from the next message.
        If that preview asks the uncommitted-work question, pass the person's
        answer as ``unsaved_work`` on both calls.
        First call without preview_digest and show the returned compatibility,
        shared-thread limits, what won't be available, and the cost line. Call again
        with the same model and that preview's expected_revision, preview_digest and
        exact declared_drops as accepted_drops: the requester must Confirm
        on the card before anything is changed. A stale preview or expired card
        changes nothing; preview again. Pass this active turn's origin_context_id.
        The same tool states the agent's own settings: ``thread_mode`` ("shared"
        to share threads where the channel allows it, admins only; or "per_caller") and
        ``required_capabilities`` (a channel that can't give one refuses the turn).
        Pass both together; an omitted one returns to the default. To change only
        settings, pass the agent's current target_backend and model.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'accepted_drops': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'items': dict({
                  'type': 'string',
                }),
                'type': 'array',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'agent_name': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'expected_revision': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'integer',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'for_everyone': dict({
            'default': False,
            'type': 'boolean',
          }),
          'model': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'preview_digest': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'required_capabilities': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'items': dict({
                  'enum': list([
                    'thread_workspace_persistence',
                    'turn_lifecycle',
                    'cancel',
                    'tool_loop',
                    'required_actions',
                    'skills_bundle',
                    'artifacts',
                    'usage_observations',
                    'reconcile',
                    'steer',
                    'tool_confirmation',
                    'native_event_replay',
                    'event_previews',
                    'vaults',
                    'memory_stores',
                    'session_resources',
                    'skills_versions',
                    'multiagent',
                    'environments_fork',
                    'native_schedules',
                    'model_request_usage',
                    'model_request_limit',
                    'input_token_limit',
                    'output_token_limit',
                    'session_spend_control',
                    'workspace_export_import',
                    'neutral_catalog',
                    'agent_delete',
                  ]),
                  'type': 'string',
                }),
                'type': 'array',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'target_backend': dict({
            'enum': list([
              'anthropic',
              'openai',
              'gemini',
              'selfhosted',
            ]),
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'thread_mode': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'enum': list([
                  'per_caller',
                  'shared',
                ]),
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'unsaved_work': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'enum': list([
                  'copy',
                  'leave',
                ]),
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'agent_name',
          'target_backend',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'request_agent_key': dict({
      'description': '''
        Give an agent an API key or token for any service: Toggl, OpenAI,
        Higgsfield, or a platform that just launched. Unknown services work too.
        <blank line>
        Never accept secret values in chat; ask for rotation if pasted. One named key
        → pass `key`. To load, upload or import a whole `.env` file of several keys at
        once, omit it. For MCP credentials use ``request_mcp_token``; GitHub access
        uses ``github_connect``, never a token.
        <blank line>
        Posts a card naming the agent and the key. Only the requester can open its
        private form; it expires in 30 minutes. Values never appear in chat. Anyone
        who talks to the agent can use added keys. Members can add new keys, including
        to built-in Daimon; replacing one a shared agent already has needs an admin.
        Pass the waiting task as `pending_task` so it resumes after the value is
        saved; call this before any clarifying question about that task, even when
        the task is underspecified.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'agent_name': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'channel_id': dict({
            'description': 'Compatibility field; origin controls the posting destination.',
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'expected_ma_agent_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'key': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': 'The exact key name (e.g. TOGGL_API_TOKEN). Pass it whenever the person named or implied ONE key. Omit ONLY when they want to upload a .env file holding several keys.',
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'pending_task': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
            'description': "The work that should run once the value is saved, in the person's words — a script, a file, a question. Omit it when they only asked to save or replace the key; the request itself is never a task.",
          }),
          'purpose': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'agent_name',
          'purpose',
          'channel_id',
          'origin_context_id',
          'expected_ma_agent_id',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'request_channel_pin_clear': dict({
      'description': '''
        Show or clear THIS channel's model-provider pin, with admin confirmation. Admin-only.
        <blank line>
        Use when an admin says "clear this channel's pin", or when a switch or refusal says
        this channel pins a provider. A pin makes every agent answer here on that provider;
        clearing it lets each agent use its own. First call without preview_digest and show
        what the channel pins. Then call again with that preview's expected_revision and
        preview_digest: the requesting admin must Confirm on the card. Only this chat's
        channel can be cleared. Existing threads keep their model. Pass this turn's
        origin_context_id. A stale preview changes nothing.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'expected_revision': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'integer',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
          'preview_digest': dict({
            'anyOf': list([
              dict({
                'type': 'string',
              }),
              dict({
                'type': 'null',
              }),
            ]),
            'default': None,
          }),
        }),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'request_fleet_config': dict({
      'description': '''
        Configure this agent's fleet of worker agents, with owner/admin confirmation.
        <blank line>
        Every agent already has a fleet with default limits (4 workers, $2 a run);
        call this only when the agent's owner or an admin asks to change or turn off
        those limits. Never use it to get around a fleet refusal or a limit someone
        else hit: tell them the limit and who can change it instead.
        <blank line>
        Use agent names, never model lists: e.g. "let this agent work with the
        research and writing agents, up to 4 workers and $2 per run". config sets
        worker_agents ("any", a list of names, or null for this agent alone),
        max_workers, budget_usd and max_worker_seconds (required for a new fleet).
        On edits, every omitted field keeps its saved value, including expiry,
        provider caps, token limits and worker selection. Explicit null removes an
        optional cap; the card marks removals. A current-settings read returns the
        complete saved config, so it can be edited without reconstructing defaults.
        Use fleet_agents to list eligible workers. Each worker runs AS that
        agent, using its own prompt, model, tools and skills; model choices
        belong in agent settings through request_agent_backend_switch.
        Worker access defaults to any agent on this server for a NEW config;
        existing grants stay unchanged until confirmed. Show every detail,
        especially worker agents, budget, expiry and provider caps.
        max_run_seconds defaults to 1200; max_turns to 1; access expires after
        90 days unless specified. No provider map means a shared budget; a
        partial map prevents omitted providers from spending.
        Omit config to show the current settings; revoke=true turns fleet off.
        Preview first. Then pass the exact returned config, expected_revision
        and preview_digest to show the requesting owner's/admin's Confirm card.
        Pass this turn's origin_context_id. A stale preview changes nothing.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        '$defs': dict({
          'FleetConfigInput': dict({
            'additionalProperties': False,
            'description': 'Chat-facing ceilings; the grant expiry and worker duration are distinct.',
            'properties': dict({
              'budget_usd': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'exclusiveMinimum': 0.0,
                    'type': 'number',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'pattern': '^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$',
                    'type': 'string',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'expires_at': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'format': 'date-time',
                    'type': 'string',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'max_input_tokens': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                    'type': 'integer',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'max_model_requests': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                    'type': 'integer',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'max_output_tokens': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                    'type': 'integer',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'max_root_turns': dict({
                'default': 3,
                'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                'type': 'integer',
              }),
              'max_run_seconds': dict({
                'default': 1200,
                'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                'type': 'integer',
              }),
              'max_turns': dict({
                'default': 1,
                'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                'type': 'integer',
              }),
              'max_worker_seconds': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                    'type': 'integer',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'max_workers': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'exclusiveMinimum': 0,
                    'type': 'integer',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'native_budget_usd': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'type': 'number',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'pattern': '^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$',
                    'type': 'string',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'native_root_budget_usd': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'type': 'number',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'pattern': '^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$',
                    'type': 'string',
                  }),
                  dict({
                    'type': 'null',
                  }),
                ]),
                'default': None,
              }),
              'provider_limits_usd': dict({
                'anyOf': list([
                  dict({
                    'additionalProperties': dict({
                      'anyOf': list([
                        dict({
                          'type': 'number',
                        }),
                        dict({
                          'pattern': '^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$',
                          'type': 'string',
                        }),
                      ]),
                    }),
                    'propertyNames': dict({
                      'enum': list([
                        'anthropic',
                        'openai',
                        'gemini',
                        'selfhosted',
                      ]),
                    }),
                    'type': 'object',
                  }),
                  dict({
