    'set_thread_model': dict({
      'description': '''
        Run this conversation on another model when the person asks in words: "use opus here", "think harder".
        <blank line>
        Only on the person's direct instruction in this conversation, never on
        your own judgement or because a model is mentioned. "Think harder" or
        "think as hard as you can" means ``opus``; ``default`` goes back to the
        agent's own model. There is no effort setting. The conversation keeps
        the choice for every later reply until someone changes it; the reply
        in progress keeps its model. Other conversations are unaffected, and
        a worker fleet (its root and every worker) always runs the agent's
        approved model.
        <blank line>
        ``origin_context_id`` must name this execution's attended origin;
        routines and other unattended runs are refused. Read the returned
        ``note`` back to the person.
      ''',
      'parameters': dict({
        'additionalProperties': False,
        'properties': dict({
          'model': dict({
            'enum': list([
              'haiku',
              'sonnet',
              'opus',
              'default',
            ]),
            'type': 'string',
          }),
          'origin_context_id': dict({
            'type': 'string',
          }),
        }),
        'required': list([
          'origin_context_id',
          'model',
        ]),
        'type': 'object',
      }),
    }),
    'set_thread_participation': dict({
      'description': '''
        Start or stop replying in a thread without being addressed each time.
        <blank line>
        Scope: ``thread_id`` from ``<thread role="current_thread">`` for a
        thread (its parent is looked up, so ``channel_id`` is optional);
        ``channel_id`` from ``<channel role="parent_channel">`` alone for a
        channel; neither for the workspace. Channel and workspace scope need an
        admin.
        <blank line>
        Modes: ``on`` follow, ``off`` do not, ``disabled`` lock a channel or
        workspace so nothing below can turn it on (not valid for a thread),
        ``inherit`` drop this scope's setting. Read the returned ``note`` back
